{{Top}}
{{Quote|In some ways, a mercenary is like a pirate without a crew. In other ways, not so much. These soldiers of fortune sign contracts with their clients in hopes of amassing great wealth, a decision I can respect. But the mercenaries most in demand are the ones who do only what they are told and ask for nothing more than the credits they were promised. While a pirate takes great pride in their independence and ambition, a mercenary has no real code and will simply fight for whomever is willing to pay them the most.|Hondo Ohnaka|<ref name="TSotBH">''[[Star Wars: The Secrets of the Bounty Hunters]]''</ref>}}
[[File:MayfeldMugshot.png|thumb|right|250px|[[Migs Mayfeld]] was a [[human]] mercenary during [[New Republic Era]].]]
A '''mercenary''', also known as a '''hired gun''' or '''soldier of fortune''',<ref name="Smuggler's Guide">''[[Star Wars: Smuggler's Guide]]''</ref> was an individual who fought for other individuals or parties in return for payment such as [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]].<ref name="Tempest Runner">''[[The High Republic: Tempest Runner]]''</ref> Mercenaries could look for work via the [[Undervine]] network.<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" /> Many [[bounty hunter]]s, like [[Cad Bane]] and [[Boba Fett]], acted like mercenaries and were hired to do jobs other than tracking down bounties.<ref name="TCW Film">[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars (film)|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' film]]</ref><ref name="HfZ">{{TCW|Hunt for Ziro}}</ref><ref name="Episode VI">{{Film|VI}}</ref>

==History==
===Republic Era===
{{Quote|You are a mercenary. Mercenaries go where they get paid. They have no personal code or&mdash;''"<br />"''Tolerance for overly chatty rust-buckets.|Pilot droid [[RL-18]] and [[Lourna Dee]]|<ref name="Tempest Runner">''[[The High Republic: Tempest Runner]]''</ref>}}
[[File:SaberForHire-CroppedCover.png|thumb|left|300px|Former Jedi Padawan Ty Yorrick took up the life of a mercenary, or "saber-for-hire," and monster hunter.]]
During the [[High Republic Era]], the former [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Ty Yorrick]] became a mercenary, sometimes referred to as a saber-for-hire, and an independent [[monster hunter]].<ref name="The Rising Storm">''[[The High Republic: The Rising Storm]]''</ref> Yorrick's career included working as a [[bodyguard]] for [[Mantessa Chekkat|Mantessa]] and [[Klerin Chekkat]].<ref name="Race to Crashpoint Tower">''[[The High Republic: Race to Crashpoint Tower]]''</ref> The [[Silver Knights]] were a group of mercenaries led by [[Captain]] [[Li Yu]].<ref name="Vow">''[[The Vow of Silver Dawn]]''</ref> The bounty hunter [[Deva Lompop]] worked as a mercenary as [[Avon Sunvale|Avon Starro]]'s bodyguard and a maurader for the [[Nihil]], before retiring and becoming an [[information broker]].<ref name="Mission to Disaster">''[[The High Republic: Mission to Disaster]]''</ref> However, she was called back into action by Jabba the Hutt.<ref name="Jabba the Hutt">[[War of the Bounty Hunters – Jabba the Hutt 1|''War of the Bounty Hunters – Jabba the Hutt'' 1]]</ref>

The mercenary droid [[AD-W4]] worked for the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] due to [[General]] [[Grievous]] hiring the droid to oversee the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatists]] operations on the [[planet]] [[Hissrich]] during the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="Mace Windu 3">[[Jedi of the Republic – Mace Windu 3|''Jedi of the Republic – Mace Windu'' 3]]</ref> In the wake of [[Jango Fett]]'s [[death]], the [[Galactic Republic]] hired the bounty hunters [[Bric]] and [[El-Les]] to train various [[clone cadet]]s.<ref name="Clone Cadets">{{TCW|Clone Cadets}}</ref>

===Imperial Era===
{{Quote|Look, I ain't in this for your revolution, and I'm not in it for you, Princess. I expect to be well paid. I'm in it for the money.|Han Solo, to Leia Organa|<ref name="Episode IV">{{Film|IV}}</ref>}}
[[File:Saponza_with_Strix.png|thumb|right|300px|Saponza, a mercenary who had been part of the underworld for decades]]
During the [[Imperial Era]], the [[Clone Force 99|Bad Batch]]&mdash;[[Hunter]], [[Tech]], [[Wrecker]], and [[Echo]], along with their young ward [[Omega]]&mdash;defected from the [[Galactic Empire|Empire]] and ended up becoming mercenaries, working directly for the [[Trandoshan]] underworld figure [[Ciddarin Scaleback]] in order to survive in the rapidly changing [[The galaxy|galaxy]] without the [[Galactic Republic|Republic]].<ref name="Rampage">{{TBB|Rampage (episode)}}</ref> Although he was from<ref name="2023 Topps">{{Topps|set=2023 Topps Star Wars|cardname=Vect Nokru|link=https://www.tcdb.com/ViewCard.cfm/sid/370777/cid/22170396/2023-Topps-Star-Wars-66-Vect-Nokru}}</ref> the peaceful world<ref name="Episode IV" /> of [[Alderaan]],<ref name="2023 Topps" /> [[Vect Nokru]] took on the life of a mercenary.<ref name="Part I">{{Kenobi|Part I}}</ref> Former [[Jedi Knight]] [[Bode Akuna]] began freelancing for [[Lank Denvik]] being a [[gunslinger]] and [[spy]].<ref name="Jedi: Survivor">''[[Star Wars Jedi: Survivor]]''</ref> The operative [[Vel Sartha]] called the criminal [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]] a mercenary when [[Luthen Rael]] brought him to worked for the [[Aldhani rebel infiltration team]].<ref name="Aldhani">{{Andor|Aldhani (episode)}}</ref> At one point during the [[Imperial Era]], [[Saponza]] found trouble getting mercenary work and suspected the issue was not just limited to him. He guessed that major syndicates like [[Crimson Dawn]] and [[Son-tuul Pride]] maintained private [[Army|armies]], leaving them no need to hire the likes of him.<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" /> Crimson Dawn had started out as a band of ruthless mercenaries before they expanded into a criminal syndicate.<ref name="Solo">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>

[[Moroff]] was a [[Gigoran]] mercenary affiliated with [[Saw Gerrera]]'s [[Partisans]]. He continued to fight with the Partisans all the way up to the [[Jedha insurgency]].<ref name="Moroff">{{Databank|moroff|Moroff}}</ref> During that insurgency, a [[Unidentified mercenary|mercenary]] guarded the [[Unidentified nomadic market|nomadic market]].<ref name="Unlock">''[[Unlock!: Star Wars Escape Game]]''</ref> [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]], disgusted at [[Han Solo]] seeming to only love [[Currency|money]] rather than wanting to help the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]], once described him as "quite a mercenary."<ref name="Episode IV" /> [[Anton Markox]] worked as a self-described "soldier of fortune" during the Imperial Era and advertised himself to crime lord clients within the ''[[Smuggler's Guide]]''.<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" />

===New Republic Era===
[[File:BaylanSkoll-Factions.png|thumb|left|250px|Baylan Skoll was a former-Jedi-turned-mercenary during the New Republic Era.]]
After its fall in the [[Battle of Jakku]],<ref name="Empire's End">''[[Aftermath: Empire's End]]''</ref> the Empire was seemingly reduced to scattered [[warlord]]s and mercenaries.<ref name="Chapter 3">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 3: The Sin}}</ref>

During the early [[New Republic Era]], [[Din Djarin]] worked as a mercenary for various organizations. The [[shock trooper]] [[Carasynthia Dune]] went into an "early retirement" when she realized that the work she was performing was not what she had enlisted for. As a result, she left the Republic and became a mercenary<ref name="Chapter 4">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 4: Sanctuary}}</ref>. Djarin's old friend [[Ranzar Malk]] formed a team composed of the ex-[[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Sniper|sharpshooter]] [[Migs Mayfeld]], the [[Devaronian]] [[Burg]], [[Twi'lek]] [[Xi'an]], and the [[droid]] [[Q9-0]], to [[Bothan-Five incident|rescue]] Xi'an's brother [[Qin]] from the ''[[Bothan-5]]'', a [[New Republic Correctional Transport]].<ref name="Chapter 6">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 6: The Prisoner}}</ref> [[Morgan Elsbeth]] had the hired gunfighter [[Lang]] working as a mercenary for her.<ref name="Chapter 13">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 13: The Jedi}}</ref> She also hired former [[Jedi Knight]] [[Baylan Skoll]] and his apprentice, [[Shin Hati]],<ref name="Part One">{{Ahsoka|Part One: Master and Apprentice}}</ref> a duo of mysterious<ref name="Ahsoka x Marvel">{{ThisWeek|9G7gNC-xXsY|Ahsoka x Marvel Comics!|sw_url=video/ahsoka-marvel-comics-this-week-in-star-wars-dispatch}}</ref> mercenaries. Both came to free her from the [[New Republic]]'s custody. She also had former [[Inquisitor|Imperial Inquisitor]] [[Marrok]] working for her.<ref name="Part One" />

A criminal named "[[Bazine Netal]]" was a mercenary who worked as a [[First Order]] [[spy]].<ref name="TFA">{{Film|VII}}</ref> The [[pirate]] [[captain]] [[Kragan Gorr]] was willing to work as a mercenary for the First Order.<ref name="Triple Dark">{{Resistance|The Triple Dark}}</ref> [[Kendoh Voss]] was a criminal of notoriety<ref name="Galaxy's Edge 5">[[Galaxy's Edge 5|''Galaxy's Edge'' 5]]</ref> active in the [[First Order-Resistance War]]. She had turned to a life of crime to restore the fortunes of her [[Kendoh Voss' family|Serennian family]]. As a criminal active as a mercenary, [[thief]],<ref name="Galaxy's Edge 2">[[Galaxy's Edge 2|''Galaxy's Edge'' 2]]</ref> and [[bounty hunter]], she would come to lead a crew known as the [[Kendoh Gang]].<ref name="Allegiance 1">[[Allegiance 1|''Allegiance'' 1]]</ref>

